  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint Programme for Rural Women&apos;s Economic Empowerment</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UN Joint Programme &#x201C;Accelerating Progress Towards Rural Women&#x2019;s Economic Empowerment&#x201D; (JP RWEE) is being implemented by FAO, IFAD, UN Women and WFP in Nepal, Niger, the Pacific Islands, Tanzania, Tunisia and Rwanda. The programme takes a holistic approach to address the multi-faceted barriers to women&#x2019;s economic empowerment, implementing diverse programme strategies that take into account intersecting forms of discrimination faced by rural women.  

The first phase of the programme was implemented between October 2014 to June 2021 in Ethiopia, Guatemala, Kyrgyzstan, Liberia, Nepal, Niger and Rwanda. A second phase of the programme was started in 2022 in Nepal, Niger, the Pacific Islands, Tanzania, Tunisia and Rwanda. The partnership seeks to tackle the barriers to gender equality and women&#x2019;s economic empowerment through holistic and integrated interventions, encompassing social, economic and political domains of empowerment. The programme aims to secure rural women&#x2019;s livelihoods, rights and resilience in order to improve nutrition and food security and contribute to equitable and sustainable food systems; increase women&#x2019;s incomes and access to decent work; increase rural women&#x2019;s participation and leadership in rural communities and institutions; and strengthen gender responsive policy environments. Critical to the interventions is the role of local and national governments and other stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
